# SRG-APP-000095-WSR-000056  -  CAT II
# The web server must produce log records containing sufficient information
# to establish what type of events occurred.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000095-WSR-000056
group:           V-206359
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-000130
control_rev5:    AU-3

contribution:    Splunk's web tier records the request method, URI and target endpoint -
                 the event type for a web transaction - in web_access.log and
                 splunkd_access.log, and the application configures that those logs are
                 written and that no endpoint is excluded.

governs:         restmap.conf - The management interface endpoints, and which clients may reach them.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           restmap.conf [] includeInAccessLog not_equals false
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] log.access_file https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] log.access_file non_empty
                 reason: "log.access_file = <filename>. The HTTP access log filename. This
                         file is written in the default $SPLUNK_HOME/var/log directory.
                         Default: web_access.log" Related shipped settings:
                         log.access_maxsize = 25000000 and log.access_maxfiles = 5.
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The record layout of the splunk_web_access and splunkd_access sourcetypes
                 is built into the product and is not a props.conf setting in the 10.4.2
                 specification, so the fields present in a written record are confirmed by
                 inspecting one.

citation:        INVENTION. Removed web.conf [settings] log.access_maxfiles min 1.
                 web.conf.spec defines it as "The maximum number of backup files to keep
                 after the web_access.log file has reached its maximum size" - a
                 rotation-retention count that has no bearing on what information each
                 record contains. The type is <integer>, so 0 is permitted, and an instance
                 keeping no backups still records the request method and URI in the current
                 log; the condition would fail a configuration that satisfies the
                 objective. Neither the check nor the fix text mentions log rotation. The
                 restmap placeholder stanza was replaced with the empty stanza the
                 determined row carries.
finding:         The web tier does not record what type of request occurred - no access log
                 is named, or a REST endpoint is excluded from splunkd_access.log - so the
                 event type for those transactions cannot be established.
